Performance:
Achieved 83.3% score on olmOCR-bench; 
Overall pass rate of 87.2% across 91 languages; 
Throughput of approximately 5 pages per second 
on RTX 5090 with vllm. Widely adopted with 50k 
combined Github stars (with Marker).

Strengths:
Unified manager for layout, recognition, and table tasks; 
Compact footprint (650M parameters) allows for edge 
deployment; v2 introduces a unified manager and more 
structured output schemas (blocks and HTML) to replace line-based outputs; 
High accuracy on mathematical expressions and complex tables.

(1) it reconstructs both text and graphics as structured outputs,
enabling more faithful document reconstruction; 
(2) it supports end-to-end training over heterogeneous document elements, allowing models to exploit semantic
relations between textual and visual components;
(3) it converts previously discarded graphics into reusable code-level supervision, unlocking multimodal
supervision embedded in existing documents.

Performance:
olmOCR-Bench: 82.4 ± 1.1; ArXiv: 83.0; 
Old scans math: 82.3; Tables: 84.9; Old scans: 47.7; 
Headers & footers: 96.1; Multi column: 83.7; 
Long tiny text: 81.9; Base: 99.7.

Achieves 94.74 overall on OmniDocBench v1.6;
 91.90 overall on MORE; 78.23 TEDS on TableVerse-5K; 
54.64 on DUDE; 861 on OCRBench; and 14.15 page-avg recall on 
CHAOS-Bench. Features a 6.37x speedup in Transformer inference
and 2.14x speedup under vLLM using DFlash acceleration.

Weaknesses:
Requires significant GPU memory; 
full benchmark across all
 document types is still limited.
